  "name": "racket-goblins",
  "description": "A Racket implementation of the Goblins distributed object-capability system, providing a secure actor-model programming environment with transactional state management. It features isolated 'vats' for state consistency, asynchronous message passing with promise pipelining, and the OCapN protocol for secure cross-network capability transport. The project facilitates decentralized, peer-to-peer coordination through cryptographic primitives and transport layers like Tor.",
